From: umurmur-esp32 <noreply@local>
Subject: [PATCH] fix: max_users check counts connecting client

Upstreamable.

Client_add() increments clientcount before Authenticate. The server-full
check used >= MAX, so the Nth connecting client saw count==N and was
rejected — effective capacity was max_users - 1.

server.c already allocates pollfds for MAX + 1 "connecting that will be
disconnected", which matches allowing count == MAX through auth.

diff --git a/src/messagehandler.c b/src/messagehandler.c
index 1af3153..ee0d349 100644
--- a/src/messagehandler.c
+++ b/src/messagehandler.c
@@ -176,7 +176,8 @@ void Mh_handle_message(client_t *client, message_t *msg)
 			goto disconnect;
 		}
 
-		if (Client_count() >= getIntConf(MAX_CLIENTS)) {
+		/* Client_count includes this connecting client (not yet authenticated). */
+		if (Client_count() > getIntConf(MAX_CLIENTS)) {
 			char buf[64];
 			snprintf(buf, 64, "Server is full (max %d users)", getIntConf(MAX_CLIENTS));
 			sendServerReject(client, buf, MUMBLE_PROTO__REJECT__REJECT_TYPE__ServerFull);
